body:
Plan: `.pi/plans/2026-09-20-scripted-session/plan.md`

Modify: `src/git.rs`

Implement a focused public function that resolves an explicitly supplied absolute checkout-root path into the existing `Checkout` type. Reuse the existing private `canonical`, `probe`, `display_name`, and `branch` helpers. Accept normal checkouts, linked worktrees, and symlinks that canonicalize to a checkout root. Reject missing/non-Git paths, bare repositories, and checkout subdirectories with contextual `anyhow` errors. Derive common repository identity and linked classification from Git output; do not scan roots, enumerate worktrees, or infer ownership from path layout.

Expected shape:
```rust
pub fn checkout(path: &Path) -> Result<Checkout> {
    let path = canonical(path)?;
    let info = probe(&path, &mut HashMap::new())
        .with_context(|| format!("inspect Git checkout {}", path.display()))?;
    // Require !info.bare and info.top.as_ref() == Some(&path), then build Checkout.
}
```
Adapt names/error text to existing conventions; do not expose `Probe`.

Reference: `src/git.rs:246-300` — existing Git probe and authoritative `validate_checkout` identity checks. Reference: `src/git.rs:410-449` — construction of linked `Checkout` values from probe facts.

Add unit tests in `src/git.rs` using temporary Git repositories for normal checkout, linked worktree, bare repository, subdirectory, non-Git path, and symlink canonicalization. Follow the existing test helpers around `src/git.rs:451-490` and keep Git subprocesses argv-based.

Acceptance: ISC-1, ISC-2, ISC-9, ISC-10, and ISC-11 are covered at the Git boundary; `cargo test git::tests` passes.

Dependencies: none.
